@startuml pipeline-status
title What is actually wired, and where the gap is

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF

rectangle "lib.rs::extractor\n#[proc_macro_derive(Extractor)]" as Entry #E8F4EA

rectangle "StructExtraction\n<&'ast DeriveInput>" as S #E8F4EA
rectangle "FieldExtraction\n<&'ast Field>" as F #FFF4E5
rectangle "SyntaxFieldAttributeExtraction\n<&'ast Attribute>" as Y #FFF4E5

rectangle "vocab suite\nflag! name_value! leaf!\nmeta_list! variants!\nnames! vocabulary! + walk" as V #E8F4EA

rectangle "Processor\n+ process_each / process_maybe" as P #E8F4EA
rectangle "Generator\n+ emit" as G #E8F4EA

rectangle "#[derive(Extractor)]\n#[source] #[from] #[with]" as DE #EEEEEE
rectangle "#[derive(Processor)]\nidentity" as DP #EEEEEE

Entry --> S : extract_from
S --> F : extract_each(data.fields.iter())

S ..> P : Extracted<..>, whole
P ..> G : Processor::Output

V ..> P : the primitives it\nwill be written against
Y ..> V : SyntaxHelper (vocabulary!)

DE ..> S : will generate
DP ..> P : will generate

note bottom of F
  Has **no fields left**. Its children were
  ""Vec<Extracted<TransformationExtraction, ..>>"",
  and that type is deleted — it was never a
  node, it held the author's transformation
  expression, which is ""#[from]"".

  Refilled by the derive (#field/children).
end note

note bottom of Y
  Works and is tested, but driven ONLY by
  base/syntax/worked.rs — never by the macro
  path. The module carries an explicit
  ""#![allow(dead_code)]"" saying so.
  (#syntax/not-driven)
end note

note bottom of P
  **Exists now.** Optional: the identity is
  derived, so downstream sees one shape.
  Cascade is bottom-up and asserted — a test
  records order and sees ["child","child",
  "parent"] with the children's OUTPUTS.
end note

note bottom of G
  **Exists now.** ""emit"" puts the stub out first
  and appends one ""compile_error!"" per reason,
  so the stub-always rule cannot be forgotten.
end note

legend right
  |<#E8F4EA>| live and tested |
  |<#FFF4E5>| works, tested, not wired |
  |<#EEEEEE>| next: the two derives |
endlegend

note as Gap
  **The gap has moved.**

  It used to be "nothing consumes the
  extraction tree" — Processor and Generator
  now exist to consume it. What is missing is
  the WIRING: lib.rs still renders top-level
  reasons and emits nothing else, and no
  concrete Processor or Generator is
  implemented for StructExtraction.

  The two derives are what close it, and
  Step 6 — rewriting the existing extractors
  onto ""#[derive(Extractor)]"" — is the test
  that the derive earns its place.
end note

Gap .. DE

note as Closed
  **#pipeline/relocate-traits is closed.**
  Extractor, Validate and Visitable now live
  in proc_macro_flow_traits, because
  ""#[derive(Extractor)]"" on a user's type means
  they must be nameable from outside.
  ""Sourced"" was deleted rather than moved.
end note

Closed .. Entry

@enduml
